From 916957313d58842bd1204cd1d6b96306a38691f7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 23:26:18 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 11/11] app: show RCS chatbot messages, their suggestions and
 the bot

A chatbot message in the conversation: R9's header and footer outside the
card (7.7.4.3, with 7.7.4.13's verified mark), a rich card vertical or
horizontal with its media, title, description and buttons, a carousel
swiped sideways, and R9's open rich card from its own widget tree
(LinearLayout with weights, TextView, ImageView, Button, View; dp taken as
a logical pixel). The chip list sits under the newest message. A text with
suggestions, an unknown type or a broken body shows the stored summary in
the usual bubble, with the chips.

Pictures (media, thumbnails, open rich card images, the bot's icon) are
fetched over HTTP(S) through the QML engine's network access into the
conversation's attachment folder (rbm/, by URL hash, up to 10 MB) and
decoded for the screen's pixels as in 0008. Video, audio and R9's iframe
play show their thumbnail and open the media outside.

Tapping a suggested reply shows it as a sent message and answers the bot.
Actions: open a URL (also R9's local browser and deep link, in the
browser), dial, a map (geo:, or the fallback URL), a calendar event (an
.ics for the calendar), a draft (into this conversation's input, or copied
for another), copy (RCC.07 copyAction, R9 clipboardAction) and R9's share
(copied: there is no share service here); the bot hears of each one that
was done. Location push, device specifics, settings and recordings say
Spacebar cannot do them.

The bot's name titles the conversation and the list, its icon is the
avatar, its description heads the chat (R9 subTitle, subImage,
subDescription), its number is the one Call dials; where R9 says the user
may not type (userInputCtrlCd, a one-way A2P sender), the input is off.
A card is copied only when it allows it (R9 7.7.4.4).

